---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout title="About TrebuchetDynamics Engineering">
  <section class="hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>TrebuchetDynamics publishes the loop, not just the output.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This site documents how TrebuchetDynamics uses validation-gated agentic
        engineering to port large Python systems to Go without losing test
        discipline or operator trust.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-visual">
      <img src="/static/go-gopher-bear-lowpoly.png" width="640" height="640" alt="Low-poly Gormes runtime mascot" />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="about-grid">
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Methodology</h2>
      <p>
        The current reference artifact is <a href="https://github.com/TrebuchetDynamics/gormes-agent">gormes-agent</a>:
        a Go-native agent runtime ported against Hermes behavior through small
        progress rows, failing tests, generated docs, and CI gates.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h2>Toolkit</h2>
      <p>
        The planned <a href="https://github.com/TrebuchetDynamics/agentic-porting-kit">agentic-porting-kit</a>
        will extract the reusable planner, builder, parity-auditor, and TDD
        skill workflows so the method can be applied outside Gormes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
